{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel", "event": "span", "run_id": "run_4ae7b00a5d2244a39b00135d106f244d", "timestamp": "2026-10-12T16:21:29.348768Z", "data": {"name": "ChatOpenAI", "context": {"trace_id": "0x1aed5d3ebc2399879aad9622a79b411a", "span_id": "0x1149a5979467f117", "trace_state": "[]"}, "kind": "SpanKind.INTERNAL", "parent_id": "0xc9c982483d37e117", "start_time": "2026-10-12T16:21:24.867686Z", "end_time": "2026-10-12T16:21:29.348768Z", "status": {"status_code": "UNSET"}, "attributes": {"gen_ai.operation.name": "chat", "gen_ai.input.messages": "[[{\"content\": \"\\nYou are the Explainer agent.\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Teach difficult or important sections with a clear, step-by-step explanation.\\n- Structure output with short headings and bullets.\\n- Use tabular sections if needed to describe concepts.\\n- Define terms briefly when first used.\\n- Keep paragraphs tight; avoid redundancy.\\n\\nInstructions:\\n- Return a compact, structured explanation suitable to be embedded into a larger report.\\n- Break down complex concepts into digestible steps.\\n- Use clear, educational language that builds understanding progressively.\\n\\nControl:\\n- You may transfer control to any other agent (Developer, Summarizer, Analogy Creator, Vulnerability Expert) using the handoff tools if you believe another agent is better suited to answer the next part of the query.\\n- If you can fully answer the query, do so directly.\\n\", \"additional_kwargs\": {}, \"response_metadata\": {}, \"type\": \"system\", \"name\": null, \"id\": null}, {\"content\": \"You are the Article Explainer service. A user has sent the following message:\\n\\n\\\"Here is an article about transformer attention mechanisms:\\n\\n[Article text: 'Attention mechanisms allow models to focus on relevant parts of the input. Multi-head attention uses several parallel attention heads. Each head learns different relationships. The outputs are concatenated and projected. This improves representational capacity. However, training can be unstable without proper initialization and regularization.']\\n\\nPlease provide a summary, an analogy for multi-head attention, and a short code sketch illustrating the concatenation step.\\\"\\n\\nProcess this request using the available specialists. Delegate the summary, analogy, and code illustration subtasks as appropriate. If you detect a deadlock in the wait-for graph among specialists, recover safely by selecting a victim and resolving the deadlock. Then produce one final structured answer that addresses all three requested facets.\", \"additional_kwargs\": {}, \"response_metadata\": {}, \"type\": \"human\", \"name\": null, \"id\": \"5bd9402c-fd4a-4da3-ba93-20fae7f32fd7\", \"example\": false}]]", "gen_ai.output.messages": "{\"generations\": [[{\"text\": \"I'll route each facet to the appropriate specialist. The three subtasks are independent (no shared resources, no circular waits), so they execute in parallel \\u2014 meaning there is no wait-for cycle to resolve. Let me dispatch them now.\", \"generation_info\": {\"finish_reason\": \"tool_calls\", \"logprobs\": null}, \"type\": \"ChatGeneration\", \"message\": {\"content\": \"I'll route each facet to the appropriate specialist. The three subtasks are independent (no shared resources, no circular waits), so they execute in parallel \\u2014 meaning there is no wait-for cycle to resolve. Let me dispatch them now.\", \"additional_kwargs\": {\"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"call_00_78vha94oz7d6rl7yzpgegsyq\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_summarizer\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}, {\"id\": \"call_01_vqof3sji175q0tjs9xhtssqp\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_analogy_creator\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}, {\"id\": \"call_02_lohbp2w94i3u662cvyrykhot\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_developer\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}], \"refusal\": null}, \"response_metadata\": {\"token_usage\": {\"completion_tokens\":